['20260627193302918954_7704a226', '20260627193302993128_e2e3c4a4'], 'kind': 
'paragraph'}], 'disclosed_conflict_ids': []}, {'title': 'Legacy and 
significance', 'section_type': 'topic', 'blocks': [{'text': 'The Ring of Nestor 
occupies a prominent place in scholarship on Aegean glyptic and religion, both 
because of the complexity of its imagery and because of the controversies 
surrounding its authenticity.[1][2][5] It has been used extensively in 
discussions of Minoan afterlife beliefs, ritual practices, and the interaction 
between Cretan and mainland elites, while also serving as a case study in the 
methodological problems posed by suspected forgeries and imperfectly documented 
finds.[2][4]', 'source_ids': ['20260627193302935626_02aac6ec', 
'20260627193302975889_96514190'], 'kind': 'paragraph'}, {'text': 'Debates over 
the ring\x19s status have contributed to wider reflections on the role of 
restorers, dealers, and scholars in shaping the archaeological record, 
especially in the early twentieth century when market conditions and the demand 
