restoration, and creative reconstruction.[2][4] In this sense, the Ring of 
Nestor is significant not only for what it may reveal about Bronze Age Aegean 
culture but also for what it illustrates about the history of archaeology and 
the critical evaluation of evidence.[2][5]', 'source_ids': 
